::DML::
The DML sublanguage is used to { ~define data structure ~control data access =manipulate data ~none of these} in a database.

::DML Commands::
Choose the DML commands
{
    ~Grant, Revoke
    ~Commit, Rollback, Savepoint
    =Insert, Update, Delete
    ~Create, Drop, Alter, Truncate, Comment, Rename
    ~None of these
}


::DML Commands::
The result of the insert command is the number of rows affected by the statement. {T}

::DML Commands::
A delete statement without a WHERE clause will delete records indiscriminately. {T}

::DML Commands::
An update statement without a WHERE clause will only update records where the specified columns are not null. {
    ~ True
    = False
}